===== LESSONS =====

--- lessons/exceptions-modules-files.md ---
# Exceptions, modules, and files

**Historical place:** Chapters 10–12, a stable consecutive block.

**Objectives:** handle invalid input; organize code into modules; read/write text or CSV data; connect persistent data to a program.

**Key content:** `try`/`except`, validation, imports, module boundaries, file paths, context managers, CSV records.

**Historical materials:** exception input labs, artwork/module exercises, word-frequency/file exercises, command-line tutorial, and Git/file exercises in newer terms.

--- lessons/inheritance-and-recursion.md ---
# Inheritance and recursion

**Historical place:** Chapters 13–14, stable in the later sequence.

**Objectives:** extend a base class appropriately; identify a recursive base case and progress step; trace and test both designs.

**Key content:** derived classes, inherited/overridden behavior, composition vs. inheritance, base case, recursive case, stack tracing.

**Historical materials:** instrument-information derived classes and Fibonacci recursion labs, plus chapter practice and pair-programming variants.

--- lessons/plotting-searching-sorting.md ---
# Plotting, searching, and sorting

**Historical place:** Chapter 16 is durable; Chapter 15 plotting is intermittent but present in spring 2024 and spring 2026.

**Objectives:** make a simple labeled plot; trace linear/binary search; implement or inspect sorting; compare growth rates qualitatively.

**Key content:** data-to-plot workflow, selection-sort trace, linear vs. binary search, sorted precondition, Big-O vocabulary and tradeoffs.

**Historical materials:** coin/sine/cosine plots, color-coded Big-O plot, selection-sort trace, and the spring 2021 homework comparing linear and binary search.

