+# Prompt 002 — CS2 Coding Odyssey spine and skeleton report
+
+## Built
+
+- `docs/grading-model.md`
+- `docs/course-ethos.md`
+- `docs/curriculum/judgment_toolkit.md`
+- `assignments/A1-weekly-coding-practice.md`
+- `assignments/A2-coding-odyssey-project.md`
+- `assignments/A5-final-reflection.md`
+- `planning/week-01.md` through `planning/week-17.md`
+
+This task did not create or edit a file under `assignments/odyssey_gates/` or
+`rubrics/odyssey_gates/`. No shared Monday Moment, Wacky Wednesday, Fun
+Friday, Paired Programming, or Show and Tell content was recreated. No
+historical placeholder file named in the prompt was edited.
+
+## What was mirrored versus adapted
+
+The following CS1 source files were read in full before their CS2 counterpart
+was written:
+
+| CS1 source read | CS2 counterpart | Mirrored |
+|---|---|---|
+| `computer_science_1/docs/grading-model.md` | `docs/grading-model.md` | Same ten categories, weights, cadence, two-axis weekly-reinforcement rubric, pair-work rule, and open-decision structure. Checkpoint descriptions were adapted to the CS2 arc. |
+| `computer_science_1/docs/course-ethos.md` | `docs/course-ethos.md` | Same course-contract voice, weekly rhythm, student artifacts, supports, build checklist, grading direction, and known-tensions shape. Shared-strand details were referenced rather than duplicated, per scope. |
+| `computer_science_1/docs/curriculum/judgment_toolkit.md` | `docs/curriculum/judgment_toolkit.md` | Same five instruments, their order, formative/rubric logic, and placement structure. Examples and placements were adapted for exceptions, modules/files, inheritance, recursion, plotting, and searching/sorting. |
+| `computer_science_1/assignments/A1-weekly-coding-practice.md` | `assignments/A1-weekly-coding-practice.md` | Same purpose, Odyssey-not-separate-problem-set model, Do list, two-axis grading, and integrity/support shape. Week map updated for CS2. |
+| `computer_science_1/assignments/A2-coding-odyssey-project.md` | `assignments/A2-coding-odyssey-project.md` | Same persistent-project spine, four-genre menu, World Bible, gate/checkpoint model, Decide/Compare, grading, and provenance sections. Checkpoint contents were adapted to the confirmed CS2 mapping. |
+| `computer_science_1/assignments/A5-final-reflection.md` | `assignments/A5-final-reflection.md` | Same purpose, five-prompt/four-category structure, permissive pass/fail language, and support/integrity section. One growth prompt gives CS2-level examples. |
+| `computer_science_1/planning/week-01.md` through `planning/week-17-finals.md` | `planning/week-01.md` through `planning/week-17.md` | Same week-title/status/focus/due planning role. CS2 skeletons intentionally retain only Weekly Focus, gate-or-checkpoint tie-in, and Due sections so they do not duplicate shared strands. |
+
+## Grounding used
+
+CS2-specific topic and depth statements were grounded in:
+
+- `docs/curriculum/course-sequence.md` and `docs/curriculum/unit-notes.md`
+  for the durable later-course sequence.
+- `docs/reports/curriculum-history-synthesis.md` for historical Coding
+  Odyssey/CYOAG, driver/navigator with AI, Coding Quest, three-problems plus
+  mini-report, and recursion-as-hardest-topic signals.
+- `lessons/exceptions-modules-files.md`,
+  `lessons/inheritance-and-recursion.md`, and
+  `lessons/plotting-searching-sorting.md` for locally documented objectives
+  and vocabulary.
+- The local Deitel PDF, *Intro to Python for Computer Science and Data
+  Science*, for the topical grounding. Its edition's printed chapter numbers
+  do not align with the prompt's confirmed chapter numbering, so the new
+  documents cite it by topic and treat Jeremy's specified CS2 map as the
+  authoritative numbering.
+
+## Open question — requires Jeremy's decision
+
+**Odyssey continuity:** the prompt asks whether CS2 students begin a new
+greater-rigor Odyssey world or formally continue their CS1 world. The
+provided direction confirms the same structure and greater depth, but not
+which continuity model applies. I did not guess. `assignments/A2-coding-
+odyssey-project.md` preserves the four-genre/new-world path conditionally and
+states the exact edit needed if formal continuation is selected. The same
+placeholder is carried into the Judgment Log and Week 2 plan.
+
+## Date and schedule handling
+
+Every planning file uses `[[DATE: week N — TBD, confirm against real CS2
+section schedule]]`. No meeting days, times, room, calendar dates, holidays,
+or finals deadline were invented.

